-- title:
--   Tate dictionary for W[3] at a multiplicative prime 3
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb Z$ and $p$ a prime with $p = 3$, and assume $W.\Delta \neq 0$, $p \mid W.\Delta$ and $p \nmid W.c_4$. Assume further that the $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $p$-torsion points of the base change of $W$ to $\mathbb Q$, taken over $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, has cardinality $p^2$. Then there exist $q_T \in \mathbb Q_p$, elements $\zeta, t$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}_p$ and an isomorphism of additive groups $\Phi \colon \mathbb Z/p \times \mathbb Z/p \to W[p](\overline{\mathbb Q})$ (the same $p$-torsion module as above) such that: $q_T \neq 0$; the nonnegative-real norm of $q_T$ equals $(p^{\,v_p(W.\Delta)})^{-1}$, with $v_p$ the $p$-adic valuation of an integer; $\zeta$ is a primitive $p$-th root of unity; $t^p$ is the image of $q_T$ under the structure map $\mathbb Q_p \to \overline{\mathbb Q}_p$; and for every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q_p}(\overline{\mathbb Q}_p)$ lying in the image, under the inclusion of the decomposition subgroup of the valuation subring of the rank-one valuation on $\overline{\mathbb Q}_p$, of its inertia subgroup, and for all natural numbers $e, c$ with $\tau\zeta = \zeta^e$ and $\tau t = \zeta^c t$, one has $\tau' \cdot \Phi(i,j) = \Phi(e\cdot i + c\cdot j,\, j)$ for all $i, j \in \mathbb Z/p$, where $\tau'$ is the image of $\tau$ under [`localGaloisToGlobal p`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L41), i.e. $\tau$ viewed as a $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphism and then restricted to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   This is the Tate parametrisation dictionary for the $3$-torsion of a curve with multiplicative reduction at $3$, transported onto the global torsion module: $\Phi(\,\cdot\,,0)$ is the line generated by the $p$-th roots of unity, and inertia shears $\Phi(0,1)$ by the Kummer character $\tau \mapsto c$ of the Tate parameter. It supplies the explicit upper-triangular inertia action used in the statements about the inertia displacement of a $3$-torsion point and about $3 \nmid v_3(\Delta)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_addEquiv_torsionBy_localGaloisToGlobal_smul_eq_of_dvd_discr_of_eq_three.lean

